# Xero Health Dashboard

Local Node.js + Express app connecting to Xero via OAuth. Runs 25 bookkeeping health checks, stores results in SQLite, renders EJS views with MTA design CSS.

## Read first
- `APP_CONTEXT.md` — how this app actually works (routes, checks, scoring, data flow)
- `DESIGN_STANDARDS.md` — MTA colors, typography, layout (use for UI; app is EJS not React)
- `CLAUDE.md` — original build spec (may differ from implementation)

## Stack
Express + EJS + `better-sqlite3` + `xero-node`. DB: `data/xero_dashboard.db`. Entry: `app.js`.

## Key files
- `src/services/xeroSync.js` — all health checks, `CHECK_DEFINITIONS`, `syncOrganisation()`
- `src/services/xeroClient.js` — `apiCall()` with token refresh and 429 retry
- `src/db/queries.js` — all SQLite operations
- `public/style.css` — MTA design tokens (`#01406A`, `#5D87FF`, 270px sidebar)

## Rules
- All Xero calls via `apiCall()` in xeroClient.js — never raw HTTP
- Paginate large fetches; 1s delay between pages for rate limits
- Health score: 100 minus 1 per check with issues; contact checks excluded from score
- 7 checks are placeholders (count 0): opening_balance_differences, invoice_or_direct, bill_or_direct, low_cost_fixed_assets, misallocated_items, unexpected_account_used, unexpected_tax_code_used
- Issue details stored as JSON in `issues.detail_json`
- No user auth — single-practice local tool
